    "narrative": "For tonight\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** stands out as our premier option with an elite 73.47 score. His matchup against Zack Littell is highly favorable, bolstered by a significant 13% platoon edge and a park factor that heavily favors his profile. While **Dylan Beavers** (61.84) and **Gavin Sheets** (62.32) provide strong efficiency against high-xERA arms like Arrighetti and Dobnak respectively, **Butler**\u2019s combination of power upside and the favorable park environment makes him the cornerstone of the LawDog outfield. We are also monitoring **JJ Bleday**, whose 61.32 score is heavily propped up by an impressive 14% park boost, though we remain wary of the negative platoon split he faces against Sugano.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Jung Hoo Lee**, who narrowly missed the cut at 46.06. While his dynamic platoon advantage against Bryan Woo provided some appeal, his current status as \"Lineup Pending\" and the general weakness of the matchup against Woo\u2019s skill profile pushed him behind the likes of **Masyn Winn** (57.07), who continues to offer sneaky SB upside against Pfaadt. We are also exercising caution with **Cal Raleigh** (54.30) and **Luis Arraez** (50.37); both are facing the stingy Logan Webb and Bryan Woo, respectively, and are subject to lineup uncertainty. **Bryce Harper** (59.49) remains a firm start despite the tough assignment against Manaea, as his high-end xwOBA maintains his floor even in a suboptimal L/L matchup. We will continue to track the final lineups for **Raleigh**, **Arraez**, and **Butler** to ensure our projections align with the actual batting orders.",
